{{Documentation}}
This template uses [[Template:AnimationViewer]] to automatically create viewers for cat and enemy pages.

==Usage==
<pre>{{UnitViewer|mode|name = (optional)|noheading = (optional)|bg = (optional)}}</pre>

<code>mode</code> is the only required parameter, and it can take the values <code>cat</code>, <code>enemy</code> and <code>conjurer</code>. Any other value will cause an error. The first two modes should be self-explanatory, but <code>conjurer</code> is used for [[:Category:Cats with Conjure ability|Cats with the Conjure ability]]. It is named "conjurer" and not "spirit" because it displays the original unit along with its spirit. In most circumstances, nothing else is needed because [[Module:UnitViewer]] uses the page name to figure out what unit it is supposed to display.

Note about conjurer: ONLY use it if the unit has exactly one spirit, and that one spirit's ID is immediately after the main cat's ID. For example [[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Master of Mind Soractes]] is fine while [[Squire Luno (Uber Rare Cat)|Squire Luno]] is not.

When the page's title cannot be used to get the unit, the unit's name must be passed to the <code>name</code> parameter. For Cats, it does not matter which form's name you use. If you do not want the "Animation" heading, pass "true" or anything to <code>noheading</code>. <code>bg</code> is also optional, and it takes a file to use as the default background just like AnimationViewer.

When a unit has a preview sprite, it will automatically have this preview added to their list of sprites. The list of all previewable cats can be found at [[Module:UnitViewer#L-9]].

==Examples==
<tabber>
Mizli=
{{UnitViewer|cat|name=Mizli|noheading=true}}
|-|Izanagi=
{{UnitViewer|conjurer|name=Daybreaker Izanagi|noheading=true}}
|-|Xenobeast Bunaglios=
{{UnitViewer|enemy|name=Xenobeast Bunaglios|noheading=true}}
|-|Bahamut Cat=
{{UnitViewer|cat|name=Bahamut Cat|noheading=true}}
</tabber>

